  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What does GLP-1 do? Why is it important?
    basic: 'GLP-1 is a hormone that indirectly helps lower blood sugar by increasing
      the production and secretion of insulin into the bloodstream after eating. '
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "GLP-1 is released from the small intestine. \nIt activates GLP-1R
      on the surface of various types of cells. \nIn beta cells, it enhances glucose
      dependent insulin secretion by more than threefold. \nGLP-1 is structurally
      and functionally like several pharmaceuticals used to treat diabetes. \nEnzymes
      break down GLP-1 quickly, but pharmaceuticals are often effective because the
      drug molecules are more stable."
  nodeSpriteLayer: []
